r_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"de78bcefa5f8c8ddee5f49c37da2216e990e972d22f8045b99b480eaa578909a","event_uuid":"fdf26552-ae52-4165-8918-37cd800d9dc8","position":{"commit_sha":"d936e917833426a70e24e80a96abaee8a59af3a0","position":"1786816238450300001-fdf26552-ae52-4165-8918-37cd800d9dc8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation started in worktree peccary-fix. Design per reviewed plan: add not_a_bug AND escalated to REASON_REQUIRED_CLASSES (escalated decided reason-required — identical structural problem: no in-repo defect fixed, verifier unpassable; reason names where it was escalated to). New REPLACEMENT_SATISFIES_REASON_CLASSES={not_a_bug,escalated}: a live replacement link is checked FIRST and still short-circuits (precedence preserved); --reason is the fallback; neither present -> write-side refusal via txn.close_class_refusal naming both doors (no fall-through to the completion verifier). RED tests first in tests/unit/commands/test_close_disposition.py.","timestamp":1786763916834653001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation complete in worktree. not_a_bug + escalated added to REASON_REQUIRED_CLASSES; new REPLACEMENT_SATISFIES_REASON_CLASSES={not_a_bug,escalated} lets a live replacement link satisfy the requirement (checked FIRST in verdict() and in the new close_disposition.reason_refusal shared by txn.close_class_refusal, which now takes optional ticket_id/tracker). Neither reason nor replacement -> write-side refusal naming both doors; never falls through to the completion verifier. ESCALATED DECISION: reason-required same as not_a_bug (identical structural problem — no in-repo defect fixed, verifier unpassable); replacement-preferred preserved via check order; --reason names where the work was escalated to. 31 new tests in tests/unit/commands/test_close_disposition.py; 738a + fc20 suites updated for the new set membership and stay green (99 passed). make lint + make typecheck clean. Docs: ticket-model.md, transition help text, cli-reference regenerated.","timestamp":1786764985014873001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed to Gerrit: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1807 (change 1807, commit eca7eba110, Change-Id Id0b80b1c0e06bc1e6eaf22c3045a1513b136a8fa). All gates green locally: make lint + make typecheck clean; 40 targeted unit tests (incl. 31 new RED-first) + 455 lifecycle interface tests pass. Two pre-existing tests pinned the OLD fall-through and were re-pinned to the new refusal: tests/unit/test_close_precheck_duplicate_link_c8fd.py scope guard (split: ordinary classes still VERIFY; not_a_bug/escalated now refused pre-LLM) and tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_link_exemptions.py (bug_supersedes_replacement/no_relation x not_a_bug rows moved VERIFY -> BLOCK_REASON). Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1; orchestrator to shepherd votes, submit, and close.","timestamp":1786775877751468001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"AC verification against MERGED main (0f34e8dc3b, Gerrit 1807, Verified +1 after environmental recheck): worktree reset to origin/main containing the merged change. (1) not_a_bug+reason no-replacement: test_reasoned_close_skips_the_verifier_and_signs_the_reason_line[not_a_bug] + test_a_reason_only_disposition_close_is_signed_with_the_reason_line PASS — verifier monkeypatch-forbidden, close_reason on the STATUS event, manifest[0]='completion-verifier: DISPOSITION not_a_bug' + class+reason line. (2) write-time refusal: test_close_without_reason_or_replacement_is_refused_naming_both_doors[not_a_bug] + test_refusal_is_enforced_below_the_cli (transition_core/close_class_refusal, gate OFF) PASS. (3) escalated: reason-required same machinery, tested by the [escalated] parametrizations + c8fd/lifecycle BLOCK-not-VERIFY re-pins; grep confirms shipped REASON_REQUIRED_CLASSES={obsolete,wontfix,not_a_bug,escalated}, REPLACEMENT_SATISFIES_REASON_CLASSES={not_a_bug,escalated}. (4) 738a + administrative + c8fd suites: 109 passed on merged tree; docs/ticket-model.md + cli-reference carry the reason-required/d54b text. (5) make lint RC=0, mypy clean (548 files) on merged tree; landed via Gerrit with both votes. All 5 AC boxes ticked. Ticket left in_progress for the orchestrator's --class close.","timestamp":1786815367305858001}],"created_at":1786750556759619001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"eb0fbee3-ca6f-4db6-8d8b-c63fbbb69e18","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"fd96-e6a0-8320-4f9b"},{"link_uuid":"0d76a9f7-8ec9-4b38-97c6-7d88a7b989f5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fc20-2df1-426e-42ab"},{"link_uuid":"6b261b06-f689-4d74-8474-aa4d55e01d33","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2b7c-eb7a-23b9-4dc8"}],"description":"## Symptom (live repro, 2026-08-14)\n`rebar transition clubby-circular-halicore open closed --class not_a_bug` on a bug whose RCA proved no defect ever existed FAILED: the close routed to the billable completion verifier, which synthesized the criterion \"bug is actually resolved: the reported defect no longer reproduces\" and marked it unmet — correctly noting \"no code change was made\" and \"the premise of the criterion (that a real defect existed and was resolved) is itself refuted by the RCA\". A truthful not_a_bug close is thus impossible without --force whenever there is no replacement ticket to link.\n\n## Mechanism\nclose_disposition.verdict() mints a deterministic disposition verdict only from find_replacement() (a live duplicates/supersedes link). not_a_bug is in DISPOSITION_CLASSES but inherently names no replacement, so verdict() returns None and the close falls through to full completion verification — which asks the wrong question for this class. The historical scoping comment (close_precheck.py ~:154) already recognizes \"not_a_bug asserts there is no defect\", but only exempted it from the duplicate-link REQUIREMENT, leaving it on the completion-verification path. escalated without a live replacement has the same fall-through shape (it \"may point outside the tracker\").\n\n## Fix (stacked on Gerrit 1794, ticket fc20 — reuse its machinery verbatim)\nMake not_a_bug a REASON-REQUIRED class exactly like obsolete/wontfix: add it to close_disposition.REASON_REQUIRED_CLASSES so (a) txn.close_class_refusal demands --reason=<text> (the RCA summary / pointer to the RCA comment), (b) verdict() mints the deterministic (class, close_reason) attestation with no replacement and no LLM, (c) decorate_manifest signs the disposition line, (d) the --reason-without---force admission in transition.py extends to it. Decide escalated deliberately: either reason-required the same way (reason = where it went), or keep replacement-preferred with reason fallback — document the choice. not_a_bug stays bug-only (NOT added to ADMINISTRATIVE_CLASSES non-bug vocabulary).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [x] A bug close --class not_a_bug --reason \"<why no defect>\" (no --force, no replacement link) closes without invoking the billable completion verifier and mints a SIGNED disposition attestation carrying class+reason (store-event + manifest tests).\n- [x] not_a_bug without --reason is refused at write time naming the requirement (gate-independent, txn.close_class_refusal test).\n- [x] escalated's no-replacement path has an explicit, tested disposition (reason-required or documented fall-through — no silent completion-verifier routing).\n- [x] 738a drift-guard and 1794's administrative-close suite stay green; docs (ticket-model.md, cli-reference) updated.\n- [x] make lint / make typecheck clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_disposition.py","reason":"add not_a_bug to REASON_REQUIRED_CLASSES; mint reason-only verdict"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_writes.py","reason":"reason persistence gating already class-driven; verify no change or extend set"},{"path":"tests/unit/commands/test_close_disposition.py","reason":"RED-first tests for not_a_bug reason-required path"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py","reason":"implementation grew: verifier bypass for reason-only dispositions (merged 1807)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition.py","reason":"write-time refusal naming --reason (merged 1807)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/txn.py","reason":"close_reason persistence in the txn seam (merged 1807)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/transition.txt","reason":"help text for --reason/--class (merged 1807)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2b7c-eb7a-23b9-4dc8"],["relates_to","fc20-2df1-426e-42ab"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"5cd227a3-4e29-4b03-9af6-361b55418327","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"d54b-1c48-dc1c-49f5","ticket_type":"bug","title":"not_a_bug close without replacement routes to completion verifier, which demands proof a nonexistent defect was fixed","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uu